+<h2>Try the connected example</h2>
+<p>Sign in to Knowledge, add a titled document and allow the worker to index it. In <strong>Cross-product handoffs</strong>, use that document ID and a request reason. Service Desk owns the resulting request; Knowledge shows destination acceptance, local job status and its own workflow separately.</p>
+<p>The mapping <code>org-a → customer-a</code> is explicit. The destination service receives create and original-receipt-read permissions, not ordinary document or Service Desk list access. A known destination commit can coexist with a failed/cancelled local attempt. An authorized <strong>Check original receipt</strong> action can reconcile it; it is not a resend.</p>
+<p>Service Desk's <strong>Request overview</strong> is a second named workspace, implemented through a lazy helper and declared CSS. It is a real multi-file assembly proof, not a second business backend.</p>
+<h2>Updating from 0.1</h2>
+<p><strong>Use a new extracted directory. Do not recursively copy over an active checkout or automatically reuse old data/configuration.</strong></p>
